# YearDots — Agent Instructions

> For AI-powered code editors (Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Windsurf, etc.)

## Project

Android lock-screen wallpaper app — 365 dots representing the year's progress.
Built with Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3, WorkManager, DataStore.

## Key Conventions

- **Single Activity**: All UI lives in `MainActivity.kt` via Compose.
- **No Fragments**: Pure Compose navigation with state hoisting.
- **Kotlin-only**: No Java files. Use Kotlin idioms (data classes, coroutines, flows).
- **Material 3**: All UI components must use `MaterialTheme` tokens.

## Package Structure

```
com.krishana.onedot
├── core/        → Business logic (WallpaperGenerator)
├── data/        → Persistence (SettingsRepository / DataStore)
├── receiver/    → BroadcastReceivers (BootReceiver)
├── ui/
│   ├── components/  → Reusable Compose screens & dialogs
│   └── theme/       → Theme, Typography, Color definitions
├── util/        → Utilities (WorkScheduler)
└── worker/      → Background workers (WallpaperWorker)
```

## Do NOT

- Use `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between()` for day-of-year — use `today.dayOfYear`
- Use `isLeapYear` boolean — use `Year.of(year).length()`
- Put `org.gradle.java.home` in project `gradle.properties`
- Load adaptive icon XML via `painterResource()` in Compose
- Use `WallpaperManager.setBitmap()` — use `setStream()` with PNG
- Schedule WorkManager before midnight (target 01:00 AM minimum)

## Do

- Keep the wallpaper text format: `"$daysLeft days left • $percent% done"`
- Compress wallpaper bitmap as PNG at quality 100
- Set wallpaper with `FLAG_LOCK` (lock screen only)
- Update `CHANGELOG.md` before every version tag
- Use spring animations for UI transitions
